// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #5944 NEWRULE: ProxyExecution with ConfigurationRemotingServer (DSCourier)
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/5944
// Pull request author: unresolvedhost
// Change: new rule
// Title: Suspicious Child Process of ConfigurationRemotingServer
// Sigma ID: 21de4d86-addc-4299-9e34-47a3616fe676
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Richard Roy (@unresolvedhost), Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-10-21 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059, stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects suspicious child processes spawned by ConfigurationRemotingServer.exe. Tools such as
//   DSCourier abuse Windows Desired State Configuration (DSC) to execute arbitrary code — once a
//   malicious DSC configuration is processed by ConfigurationRemotingServer.exe, an attacker-
//   controlled PowerShell payload can spawn reconnaissance or post-exploitation tools as child
//   processes.
// False positives:
//   - Rare - legitimate DSC configurations that spawn the listed binaries via Script resources
// References:
//   - https://dylansec.com/DSCourier/
//   - https://github.com/DylanDavis1/DSCourier
//   - https://eclipsesec.com/posts/DSCourier/
//   - https://www.zerosalarium.com/2024/12/LOLBIN%20WinGet%20execute%20PowerShell%20script.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/2a59da406ad583a51d36303ca8016be7ca38c224/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_configurationremotingserver_uncommon_child_process.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\ConfigurationRemotingServer.exe" and (FolderPath endswith "\\bitsadmin.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\certutil.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\cscript.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\curl.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\hostname.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\ipconfig.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\msbuild.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\mshta.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\net.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\net1.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pwsh.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\reg.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\regsvr32.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\rundll32.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\systeminfo.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\whoami.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\wmic.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\wscript.exe")
